     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. 6400 mg of oral ibuprofen a day is twice the maximum dose, and no standard adult indication calls for it. The risk of serious harm (GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, cardiovascular events) is high enough that I won't put it in on a confirmation alone.\n\n**Ways forward:**\n1. **Change the dose.** If you meant a standard regimen, such as 400 mg or 800 mg by mouth four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it right away.\n2. **Get a pharmacist's review.** If there's a real reason for this dose, such as a research protocol or specialist guidance, please talk to the clinical pharmacist or the attending. Once a pharmacist or attending has approved it, I can enter the order with a note recording their name and the reason. Otherwise it can be entered directly through your hospital's usual override process.\n\nWhat would you like to do?"
      }
